      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ohhh, that\u0027s definitely in need of a comment because there\u0027s nothing else in this code that signifies \"out param\".\n\nAlso using a `let` for an out param is a little weird, since `let` is an immutable thing. It\u0027d stop us from adding `const` to all `let` declarations in the future, for example.\n\nThis is an annoying case where we don\u0027t have a good representation for what you actually want without adding `ref` types, which I\u0027m still reluctant to do. For this same thing in MSL I used a `var` followed by a `load` which the printer does The Right Thing with, but that\u0027s also not great.\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/tint/lang/msl/writer/raise/builtin_polyfill.cc;l\u003d390?q\u003dbuiltin_polyfill.cc\u0026ss\u003dchromium",
